    "created_at": "2022-01-12T12:41:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-01-12T12:42:27Z",
    "body": "it shouldn't be restricted. \r\n\r\nwithout further context to the markup pattern shown here, i could easily imagine other semantically appropriate elements that could have been used.  But, the example provided doesn't seem like it should be invalid, and in fact could be perfectly reasonable to do.\r\n\r\nAs an example why: a fieldset could contain functional controls in one view (an edit mode), and then after editing the controls might become static text (similar to the OP example).  That is fine / valid.  It helps maintain a consistent aural dom structure.\r\n\r\nIn effect, the end user is encountering a section of content that is announced as a `role=group` with an accessible name of `contact details`.  Again, without context of the full document I'm not sure if that's what is appropriate for the OP's situation.  But, if not, then different markup is the answer - not revising what's allowed within a fieldset.\r\n\r\n@untitaker brings up more reasons to expand on why the content model shouldn't be restricted, and why what's here is valid.  Note: that a fieldset, or its descendant form controls, can be programmatically associated with a form ... so even a fieldset's use outside of a ancestor from might be necessary / would be fine in some situations.",
